{"id": "EUVD-2026-96696", "enisaUuid": "1ae16e49-0af0-326a-8fae-631b51fd2b63", "description": "ImageMagick on Windows through 7.1.2-33 and 6.9.13-58 contains an uncontrolled search path vulnerability in NTGhostscriptEXE() that launches gswin64c.exe by bare name when Ghostscript is unregistered. Attackers can plant a malicious gswin64c.exe in the working directory to execute code with ImageMagick privileges when PDF, PostScript, or EPS files are converted.", "datePublished": "2026-10-11T01:35:43", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-13T19:53:08", "baseScore": 7.3, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:L/AC:H/AT:P/PR:N/UI:P/VC:H/VI:H/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/ghostx-86/exploitarium/tree/main/imagemagick-gs-delegate-hijack-poc", "https://github.com/ImageMagick/ImageMagick/blob/211e5b975a0019a88dcef5f84c1193f46738d815/MagickCore/nt-base.c#L1469-L1511", "https://github.com/ImageMagick/ImageMagick/blob/211e5b975a0019a88dcef5f84c1193f46738d815/MagickCore/nt-base.c#L2829-L2832", "https://github.com/ImageMagick/ImageMagick", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/imagemagick-through-7.1.2-33-and-6.9.13-58-uncontrolled-search-path-via-ghostscript-delegate"], "aliases": ["GHSA-92c8-5jfq-j2vj", "CVE-2026-108693"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.13, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "d1746910-eb53-33fd-b5a3-3be548cde4b3", "product": {"name": "ImageMagick", "vendor": {"name": "ImageMagick"}}, "product_version": "7.0.0-0 \u22647.1.2-33"}, {"id": "e63e7f3a-ea46-373d-baa0-0843f405a461", "product": {"name": "ImageMagick", "vendor": {"name": "ImageMagick"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22646.9.13-58"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "66ba456c-ff56-32a0-93a9-96453c64db83", "vendor": {"name": "ImageMagick"}}], "isExploited": false}